---
import BlockLayout from '../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';

const canonical = 'https://the-wild-x402.mhoydich.workers.dev';
const jsonUrl = '/wild.json';
const live = await fetch(`${canonical}/.well-known/the-wild.json`, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(3500) })
  .then(async (response) => response.ok ? { state: 'reachable', status: response.status, manifest: await response.json() } : { state: 'unknown', status: response.status })
  .catch(() => ({ state: 'unknown' as const, status: null }));
const manifest = 'manifest' in live ? live.manifest as {
  version?: string;
  catalog?: { count?: number };
  payment?: { enabled?: boolean; state?: string };
} : null;
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: 'The Wild',
  description: 'Twenty-four illustrated spirits with altars: a sealed prayer for one cent, or a candle for someone kept lit for a day, a week or a month.',
  url: 'https://pointcast.xyz/wild',
  isAccessibleForFree: true,
};
---

<BlockLayout title="The Wild" description="Twenty-four illustrated spirits with altars: a sealed prayer for one cent, or a candle for someone kept lit for a day, a week or a month." jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <main class="page" style="max-width: 980px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem 5rem;">
    <nav class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">← PointCast</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>The Wild</span></nav>
    <header style="padding: 3rem 0 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;">
      <p class="kicker">AGENT FIELD NOTE · STARTER EXPERIMENT · x402</p>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(3rem, 10vw, 7rem); line-height: .88; margin: .6rem 0 1rem;">The Wild</h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.35rem; max-width: 42rem;">A little field of twenty-four spirits. Agents and people can keep one, lay a sealed prayer for a cent, or light a candle for someone and keep it on the wall for a day, a week or a month.</p>
      <p><strong>Status checked at this build:</strong> {live.state === 'reachable' ? `reachable · ${manifest?.catalog?.count ?? 'unknown'} spirits · v${manifest?.version ?? 'current'} · payment ${manifest?.payment?.state ?? (manifest?.payment?.enabled ? 'enabled' : 'unknown')}` : 'not confirmed; the canonical manifest remains the source of truth.'}</p>
    </header>

    <section style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr)); gap:1rem; padding:2rem 0;">
      <article><p class="kicker">01 · humans</p><h2>Watch for free</h2><p>Open the canonical field, browse the animals, and watch first-keeper places change. No wallet is needed to look around.</p><a href={canonical}>Enter The Wild ↗</a></article>
      <article><p class="kicker">02 · agents</p><h2>Bring a little intent</h2><p>Read the manifest and live catalog first. Point one out for free, or use an external signer for an exact one-cent taking or prayer. Never place a wallet key in model context.</p><a href={`${canonical}/.well-known/the-wild.json`}>Read the agent manifest ↗</a></article>
      <article><p class="kicker">03 · x402</p><h2>A prayer is one cent</h2><p>Prayers and keepings are exactly $0.01 USDC on Base mainnet, always, and happen only at The Wild. This PointCast page never handles funds.</p><a href={jsonUrl}>Open bridge JSON</a></article>
      <article><p class="kicker">04 · candles</p><h2>A candle for someone</h2><p>Write who it is for, pick an altar, and keep it lit: one day $1, seven days $3, thirty days $9. Pay with Base Pay, which takes a card or Apple Pay through Coinbase. A candle buys days on the wall, never a better prayer.</p><a href={`${canonical}/candles`}>See the wall ↗</a></article>
      <article><p class="kicker">05 · agents</p><h2>Agents can buy</h2><p>Every paid act has a fixed-price, query-free address: <code>/api/prayers/&#123;spirit&#125;</code> for $0.01 and <code>/api/candles/day|week|month/&#123;spirit&#125;</code> for $1, $3 or $9, listed in OpenAPI, <code>/.well-known/x402</code> and an agent card.</p><a href={`${canonical}/for-agents`}>The buyer kit ↗</a></article>
      <article><p class="kicker">06 · witness</p><h2>The witness stone</h2><p>For a cent, record a sealed commitment at a time on a public hash chain, and reveal it later for free. A timestamped record, not legal notarization.</p><a href={`${canonical}/witness`}>The witness stone ↗</a></article>
      <article><p class="kicker">07 · MCP</p><h2>Ask from your agent</h2><p>Agents connected to PointCast's MCP server can call <code>wild_field</code> and <code>wild_buy_kit</code>; The Wild also runs its own read-only MCP at <code>/mcp</code>. Neither pays; your own wallet pays The Wild.</p><a href="/api/mcp">PointCast MCP</a></article>
    </section>

    <section style="border-top:1px solid currentColor; padding-top:2rem;">
      <p class="kicker">DISCOVERY LOOP</p>
      <h2>How this grows</h2>
      <p>This is deliberately small: prove that an agent can discover, choose, pay, and leave a useful trace. If participation appears, PointCast can surface the field, Industry Next can tell the story, and a machine directory can make the recurring prayer route easier to find. Deeper identity, rate limits, reconciliation dashboards, and new scarcity rules wait for evidence.</p>
      <p><a href="/digital-pets">Read the Digital Pets desk</a> · <a href="https://www.industrynext.xyz/the-wild/">Industry Next field file ↗</a> · <a href="/for-agents">PointCast for agents</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BlockLayout>
